In ASP.NET Core, middleware runs strictly in the order it is added in Program.cs, and correct ordering is essential—for example, UseRouting() must come before UseAuthorization(), 
and UseAuthentication() must always precede UseAuthorization() .
Why Middleware Order Matters
The pipeline is executed top‑to‑bottom for requests and bottom‑to‑top for responses.
Each middleware can short‑circuit the pipeline.
Misordering causes issues like broken CORS, missing authentication, wrong client IPs, or HTTPS redirect loops. 

var app = builder.Build();

app.UseExceptionHandler("/error");
app.UseHsts();

app.UseForwardedHeaders();
app.UseHttpsRedirection();

app.UseStaticFiles();

app.UseRouting();

app.UseCors();

app.UseAuthentication();
app.UseAuthorization();

app.MapControllers();

app.Run();
